{
  "result": "The owned-wire DATA candidate passes existing functional coverage and has lower same-order normalized medians in both process pairs. Improvement magnitude is not stable across the two orders; the public route still loses to the manual peer in both candidate processes.",
  "head_at_packaging": "f3ad2e4de2f6eedddd5ec7d74a9d54eff452fc98",
  "product": {
    "file": "src/io_http2/http2.cc",
    "changed": "DATA read callback sets NO_COPY instead of copying into nghttp2 payload storage. The new synchronous send-data callback accepts the complete header/payload/padding into the existing owned wire and returns PAUSE.",
    "completion": "mem_send2 returning zero with a queued wire is treated as one encoded frame; candidate_epoch and queued_for_flush are preserved, and flushed_epoch advances only after original transport completion.",
    "lifetime": "Borrowed source, operation pins, EOF/trailer and stream-close lifetimes remain. Native callback performs no transport I/O/yield/reentrant native call. Partial-cancel tails remain owned by the original wire buffer.",
    "errors": "If native reports callback failure, an existing fatal_status (including callback wire OOM) takes precedence over the generic native error mapping.",
    "unchanged": "Control-frame route, public API/ABI/options, allocator, transport partial writes/read assistance/cancellation/deadline, dependency, peer, warmup and timing fixture are unchanged. Empty-notify micro-candidate was not included.",
    "copy_scope": "This is not zero-copy: DATA still copies once from borrowed source to owned wire. One native-bounce payload copy is removed by source construction, not by a new runtime copy counter. No native-workspace or total allocation reduction is claimed."
  },
